# Normalize line endings to LF for text files, regardless of platform or a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Prettier's default (endOfLine: "lf",
# unset in .prettierrc.json) expects LF on disk. Without this file, a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF on
# checkout, and `npm run ci`'s format:check then flags those files as needing
# formatting even though their actual content matches HEAD exactly — a line-ending
# artifact, not real drift. See git history around 2026-09-11 for the incident this
# fixes: files reformatted to "fix" it showed an empty `git diff`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never run line-ending normalization or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
